WEBVTT

00:01.860 --> 00:06.530
#39: EMBRACING YOUR AMBITIONS
IN THE LIGHT PART 4

00:06.530 --> 00:07.450
Sunraku.

00:09.240 --> 00:12.450
About my ultimate that
I can activate after landing

00:12.450 --> 00:15.330
Apocalypse and Catastrophe
five times each...

00:16.120 --> 00:17.370
Actually...

00:18.040 --> 00:19.210
Actually?

00:21.250 --> 00:25.590
Actually, it also needs
a long chant to activate.

00:26.460 --> 00:27.610
Chant?

00:28.550 --> 00:31.680
Not only that, but immediately
after I finish the chant,

00:32.180 --> 00:34.100
I must hit Lycagon with it.

00:36.030 --> 00:39.760
So even after fulfilling the requirements,
we still have obstacles to overcome, huh?

00:40.840 --> 00:43.230
The skill is a lot of
hassle to use, indeed.

00:43.770 --> 00:46.850
But in exchange,
I can guarantee its force.

00:47.440 --> 00:48.860
All right.

00:48.860 --> 00:51.450
It's not like I have no plan at all.

00:51.850 --> 00:55.240
But if it doesn't work
even with our best efforts...

00:56.950 --> 01:00.080
...let's laugh it off and beat
this area again from the start.

01:02.080 --> 01:03.000
Right!

01:04.920 --> 01:08.880
With over thirty million
players worldwide,

01:08.880 --> 01:11.970
it reigns supreme over
all Full-Dive VR games.

01:11.970 --> 01:15.470
In Shangri-La Frontier,
known as a god-tier game,

01:16.010 --> 01:16.600
THE SEVEN COLOSSI

01:16.600 --> 01:18.980
THE SEVEN COLOSSI
there exist Unique Monsters

01:18.980 --> 01:21.390
THE SEVEN COLOSSI
called "The Seven Colossi."

01:22.340 --> 01:27.230
One of them is Lycagon the Nightslayer.

01:28.110 --> 01:31.700
I'm nothing like the last time!

01:31.700 --> 01:36.740
I'll show you the power
of a level-99 player!

01:49.920 --> 01:56.220
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

03:09.170 --> 03:10.750
Apocalypse!

03:20.850 --> 03:23.310
The requirements were fulfilled.

03:27.930 --> 03:31.520
I am the harnesser of chaos.

03:31.520 --> 03:33.860
- Above the clouds,
- Rei's ultimate requires

03:33.860 --> 03:35.820
- flying to the edge of heaven.
- a long chant to cast.

03:35.820 --> 03:38.530
They will be defenseless
during that, of course.

03:38.530 --> 03:41.030
I gotta protect them at all costs.

03:44.040 --> 03:46.790
Now's time for the climax!

03:46.790 --> 03:49.880
Come at me, you mutt!

03:57.430 --> 03:58.970
The moon!

03:58.970 --> 04:02.930
It's only been a few minutes
since I put Suzaku on standby!

04:02.930 --> 04:05.430
This is the worst timing.

04:06.560 --> 04:08.770
You picked now to laugh at us, RNG goddess?

04:08.770 --> 04:10.390
RANDOM NUMBERS
You picked now to laugh at us, RNG goddess?

04:19.910 --> 04:21.740
Watch out, Akitsuakane!

04:21.740 --> 04:24.540
She'll attack with an invisible clone
in the dark!

04:24.540 --> 04:25.540
What?!

04:25.540 --> 04:28.120
Listen well to the sound
it makes to dodge it!

04:28.120 --> 04:30.500
No, that won't be enough.

04:31.460 --> 04:36.510
If we run, then Rei will be targeted.

04:37.720 --> 04:42.510
And if she takes Rei down,
we'll lose our means of winning.

04:44.980 --> 04:46.460
Mr. Sunraku?

04:48.100 --> 04:49.020
This means...

04:49.890 --> 04:53.520
Unless we neutralize
the invisible clone itself...

04:54.190 --> 04:55.860
...we're going to lose.

04:59.530 --> 05:03.450
Invisible clones... in the dark...

05:04.490 --> 05:08.450
Deep below,
I navigate the bottom of the abyss.

05:08.450 --> 05:14.020
Hizutome, should I continue
chanting like this?

05:14.680 --> 05:17.800
Should I cancel my chant
and focus on evading?

05:18.300 --> 05:21.050
Keep chanting, please, Psyger-0!

05:22.050 --> 05:24.850
Let us deal with the invisible clones!

05:24.850 --> 05:25.810
Indeed!

05:29.850 --> 05:30.810
Got it!

05:31.770 --> 05:34.190
I'm counting on you, Akitsuakane!

05:37.610 --> 05:43.010
Deep below, I navigate
the bottom of the abyss.

05:52.210 --> 05:54.140
I can hear it.

05:54.690 --> 05:57.190
The faint sound of something
rubbing against the ground.

05:57.780 --> 06:01.220
If it's hiding in the dark,
then I just have to light it up!

06:01.800 --> 06:04.590
Hagakushi Hidden Secret Arts!

06:10.980 --> 06:12.980
FEARSOME DRAGON BREATH
Fearsome Dragon Breath!

06:21.150 --> 06:25.990
"Fearsome Dragon Breath" is one
of the Hidden Arts obtained at random

06:25.990 --> 06:31.250
after finishing the training quests
needed to acquire the Ninja job.

06:31.250 --> 06:33.710
It is a secret ninja art that imitates

06:33.710 --> 06:36.920
the breath of a dragon
vividly in the player's memory.

06:36.920 --> 06:37.630
And...

06:38.590 --> 06:43.220
Akitsuakane, who has only
played for less than a month,

06:43.220 --> 06:45.050
has only encountered one dragon.

06:46.180 --> 06:48.010
The force of the Fearsome

06:48.010 --> 06:48.890
Dragon Breath she obtained

06:48.890 --> 06:49.970
SIEGWURM THE SKY RULER
Dragon Breath she obtained

06:49.970 --> 06:51.970
SIEGWURM THE SKY RULER
was nothing but a cheap imitation

06:51.970 --> 06:55.520
SIEGWURM THE SKY RULER
of the Sky Ruler's.

06:55.520 --> 06:56.150
However...

06:57.440 --> 06:59.520
It suffices as a light source!

07:00.270 --> 07:03.530
My eyes have laid sight on thee!

07:04.280 --> 07:07.410
Behold, Night Emperor!

07:07.410 --> 07:08.950
Taste my Bamboo Lightning!

07:08.950 --> 07:11.160
BAMBOO LIGHTNING
Taste my Bamboo Lightning!

07:18.750 --> 07:21.000
Y-You stopped her!

07:21.000 --> 07:22.630
Great job, Ceecrue!

07:23.050 --> 07:24.670
We did it!

07:24.670 --> 07:29.010
As long as I know where she'll be coming from,
I can solidify it even further.

07:29.930 --> 07:31.310
But goodness me.

07:31.310 --> 07:35.230
To think that the Night Emperor's
weakness was light all along.

07:35.890 --> 07:39.810
You're doing much better
than I expected, Akitsuakane!

07:39.810 --> 07:41.770
Hurry up, Mr. Sunraku!

07:45.530 --> 07:47.280
The two-faced heavenly devil

07:47.280 --> 07:50.990
stretching out their arms
to reach the farthest point.

07:52.010 --> 07:54.120
Now it's our turn.

07:54.870 --> 07:56.540
I've got to nail this right.

07:57.790 --> 08:00.320
O great enemy blocking my high road.

08:01.040 --> 08:03.310
I still need a few more seconds
to finish my chant.

08:03.310 --> 08:04.620
Until then...

08:04.620 --> 08:07.680
I'm counting on you, Hizutome!

08:15.180 --> 08:19.190
No one may tread upon
this mighty path before I.

08:22.480 --> 08:24.940
I'm your opponent!

08:25.420 --> 08:27.820
Mr. Sunraku! Mr. Sunraku! Mr. Sunraku!

08:27.820 --> 08:29.570
Calm down, Emul.

08:29.570 --> 08:32.660
I've finished preparing for my trump card.

08:37.000 --> 08:40.710
Now, let's break it out, Gilta Brille!

08:40.710 --> 08:45.840
Show her what you really can do!

08:47.210 --> 08:50.380
Here we go! Crystal Bullet activate!

08:53.850 --> 08:55.430
Growing-up!

09:00.940 --> 09:02.980
Emul! Right front leg!

09:02.980 --> 09:03.650
Yessir!

09:04.150 --> 09:07.230
Mana Shaker!

09:12.410 --> 09:14.700
Good! That dealt damage!

09:14.700 --> 09:16.660
It's a direct hit!

09:16.660 --> 09:19.660
Now, I'm counting on you.

09:19.660 --> 09:21.670
This is your final job.

09:21.990 --> 09:23.170
Suzaku!

09:23.580 --> 09:25.290
Marking target point.

09:25.290 --> 09:27.050
MARKING TARGET POINT

09:27.920 --> 09:28.630
Activating Incinerating Slasher.

09:28.630 --> 09:29.630
INCINERATING SLASHER
Activating Incinerating Slasher.

09:29.630 --> 09:30.420
INCINERATING SLASHER - ACTIVATE
Activating Incinerating Slasher.

09:35.430 --> 09:37.310
Slam it down!

09:40.560 --> 09:41.810
Well done, Suzaku!

09:41.810 --> 09:43.190
REMAINING ENERGY
Well done, Suzaku!

09:44.400 --> 09:46.440
Take a rest for now.

10:04.360 --> 10:06.460
Emul, you should drop back.

10:06.460 --> 10:07.210
Huh?

10:07.670 --> 10:10.210
Now it's time for my trump card.

10:11.010 --> 10:12.220
Mr. Sunraku!

10:13.840 --> 10:17.930
Gilta Brille's right hand
has the ability to charge up

10:17.930 --> 10:20.600
magical energy from
getting exposed to moonlight.

10:21.060 --> 10:27.370
That power is needed to generate
the crystal bullets on the left hand.

10:27.370 --> 10:31.360
But it can also be used in another way.

10:34.740 --> 10:40.620
And that is a mechanism that converts
all charged-up energy into a destructive force.

10:41.120 --> 10:42.790
Exceed Charge!

10:43.370 --> 10:45.880
EXCEED CHARGE

10:46.200 --> 10:51.710
Once used, it takes a whopping
168 hours to recharge.

10:51.710 --> 10:55.430
In other words,
I can only use this once a week.

10:55.430 --> 10:57.720
A special finisher move!

10:58.390 --> 10:59.140
But...

11:01.580 --> 11:05.690
...its trait of dealing more damage
the more magical energy you charge up

11:05.690 --> 11:11.170
generates enough destructive power to
more than make for its disadvantages!

11:11.570 --> 11:16.280
If you're avoiding the moon,
I'll slam it into your face!

11:18.780 --> 11:24.290
I'm busting out all
the moonlight magical energy

11:24.290 --> 11:27.000
I've been building up
throughout this battle!

11:29.290 --> 11:34.590
Exceed Charge: Reject!

11:37.510 --> 11:40.010
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

11:41.010 --> 11:41.760
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

11:41.760 --> 11:44.430
Exceed Charge...

11:46.520 --> 11:48.850
Reject!

11:48.850 --> 11:50.270
EXCEED CHARGE: REJECT
Reject!

11:50.270 --> 11:51.520
EXCEED CHARGE: REJECT

11:55.030 --> 11:57.400
This is my payback for that night!

11:59.730 --> 12:02.660
You better accept it!

12:20.530 --> 12:23.680
There's one more reason,
besides its long recast time,

12:23.680 --> 12:26.660
I'm treating Exceed Charge: Reject
as my trump card.

12:27.640 --> 12:30.190
All right, here comes the rebound.

12:47.500 --> 12:49.330
SUNRAKU
GUTS

12:49.770 --> 12:52.090
In exchange for its massive power,

12:52.090 --> 12:55.340
the user winds up taking
a huge amount of rebound damage.

12:55.720 --> 12:57.840
- Sunraku!
- Mr. Sunraku!

12:59.840 --> 13:04.390
I managed to avoid getting insta-killed,
thanks to my Guts.

13:04.850 --> 13:10.730
But if I can't avoid this impact,
it'll be over for me either way!

13:11.350 --> 13:13.360
I gotta escape to Inventoria.

13:13.360 --> 13:16.940
No, it's no use. Even if I teleport,
it won't kill my momentum.

13:16.940 --> 13:20.150
I'll just bash into the wall
over there and die.

13:20.820 --> 13:23.870
I didn't expect the rebound
to be this massive.

13:23.870 --> 13:28.750
Damn it! Am I seriously gonna
bow out like this right at the climax?!

13:28.750 --> 13:31.000
Magic Chain!

13:31.000 --> 13:31.870
Huh?

13:42.720 --> 13:44.390
Y-You guys!

13:44.800 --> 13:47.390
Thank goodness! You're still alive!

13:47.390 --> 13:49.390
You're saved!

13:51.560 --> 13:53.270
A harrowing scrape, verily.

13:55.150 --> 13:56.900
Thanks, guys.

13:56.900 --> 14:00.430
I was about to miss out
on Rei's big moment.

14:01.400 --> 14:04.910
All right!
We've all set the table for you, Rei!

14:05.990 --> 14:08.410
Show us what maximum power looks like!

14:17.000 --> 14:22.050
And so, my strike shall
pulverize all in my way.

14:23.510 --> 14:26.930
I am the Satanael of the heavens.

14:27.640 --> 14:29.810
And the Satan of hell.

14:29.810 --> 14:36.150
This skill is hard to pull off and the battle
often ends before I can even use it.

14:36.150 --> 14:38.980
I thought this skill had no practical use.

14:39.530 --> 14:42.860
I bring two into one
to execute chaos.

14:42.860 --> 14:44.280
But not now.

14:48.120 --> 14:52.660
It's something that must exist
for this moment everyone made for me.

14:55.580 --> 14:58.670
To strike down the Night Emperor!

15:10.930 --> 15:13.930
Chant the twilight of the beginning.

15:30.330 --> 15:31.950
Armageddon!

15:42.340 --> 15:44.720
ARMAGEDDON

15:53.220 --> 15:55.640
So this is... Rei's ultimate!

15:55.640 --> 15:57.600
A-Amazing...

15:58.730 --> 16:00.270
Armageddon...

16:00.980 --> 16:03.110
What an insane skill!

16:18.580 --> 16:21.000
Y-You did it!

16:21.500 --> 16:24.300
You did it, Psyger-0!

16:24.300 --> 16:26.800
I'm sure getting hit with that would—

16:41.980 --> 16:43.560
You've got to be kidding me!

16:48.700 --> 16:50.860
N-No way...

16:52.370 --> 16:56.870
Even that... still wasn't enough?!

17:02.000 --> 17:03.170
Rei!

17:05.800 --> 17:07.800
Emul! Can you use Mana Shaker?

17:07.800 --> 17:10.510
I-It'll take a bit longer!

17:23.570 --> 17:25.070
Mr. Sunraku...

17:25.070 --> 17:27.400
What's that?!
Is she traversing the shadow?

17:27.400 --> 17:29.190
No, not that.

17:29.190 --> 17:34.320
This... Lycagon's body...
Is it falling apart?

17:35.240 --> 17:37.580
Mr. Sunraku! Look at that!

18:15.990 --> 18:19.330
What was that just now?

18:19.330 --> 18:21.830
I saw Lycagon's face for a moment.

18:21.830 --> 18:24.370
It looked like she was smiling.

18:34.010 --> 18:36.260
TITLE "SHADOW WOLF PENETRATOR" OBTAINED
UNIQUE CONDITION "GUIDING TORCH" OBTAINED

18:36.260 --> 18:38.510
BEGIN UNIQUE SCENARIO EX "THE TORCH OF COURAGE
THAT BANISH THE DARKNESS OF NIGHT"?

18:39.390 --> 18:41.020
Our rewards!

18:41.020 --> 18:44.230
This means we won!

18:44.230 --> 18:45.520
Y-Yeah...

18:45.910 --> 18:49.570
But this is not the result
screen for beating Lycagon.

18:49.570 --> 18:53.530
Besides, what was that face
in the darkness?

18:53.530 --> 18:56.780
TITLE "SHADOW WOLF PENETRATOR"
OBTAINED

18:57.370 --> 18:58.780
Shadow wolf...

19:01.660 --> 19:04.830
I see. Now I get it.

19:04.830 --> 19:06.250
What is it?

19:06.250 --> 19:10.880
I think the one we thought
was the real deal

19:10.880 --> 19:16.550
was a "shadow wolf" created by her.
In other words, a clone.

19:17.390 --> 19:18.050
Oh my!

19:18.680 --> 19:22.180
The real one was either watching from afar

19:22.180 --> 19:25.480
or was having fun controlling
the clone, I suppose?

19:25.480 --> 19:29.060
No way... So it was a fake?

19:30.360 --> 19:35.320
Damn it! How much does that darn mutt
enjoy making fools out of us?!

19:35.320 --> 19:36.570
What does it matter?

19:37.530 --> 19:43.290
Fake or not, nobody has ever
faced up to Lycagon before.

19:43.790 --> 19:45.210
But with Hizutome...

19:45.710 --> 19:49.460
But with all your help,
we were able to drive her away.

19:49.460 --> 19:50.260
That, for me...

19:50.880 --> 19:53.460
...was a whole lot of fun!

19:55.330 --> 19:57.220
Hmm? What's this?

19:57.220 --> 19:59.470
I think I just saw something...

20:03.140 --> 20:07.020
But yeah, Rei's right.

20:07.020 --> 20:10.520
I get to go on an adventure
with Hizutome! I'm so happy!

20:12.280 --> 20:17.950
Just seeing that crazy Armageddon
was worth all the effort.

20:19.990 --> 20:22.120
Yeah, that was certainly amazing!

20:22.120 --> 20:25.870
Shadow or clone or whatever,
a win is still a win!

20:25.870 --> 20:31.250
This means I've got my revenge
against that hated Lycagon!

20:31.250 --> 20:33.630
Yeah! You did it!

20:33.630 --> 20:35.550
Hooray!

20:36.340 --> 20:38.130
H-Horray!

20:38.130 --> 20:42.760
All right. We can go pay our respects
to the real one some other time!

20:42.760 --> 20:45.770
Looks like we've got some rewards,
so let's see what we got...

20:46.710 --> 20:48.020
Huh?

20:48.020 --> 20:52.270
Lycagon's Mark on you is
looking weird, Mr. Sunraku.

20:52.270 --> 20:54.150
Wh-What's this?!

20:56.650 --> 20:59.150
Oh, I see! This is...!

20:59.150 --> 21:00.660
LYCAGON'S MARK

21:03.620 --> 21:08.250
Although it was a shadow clone, it was
that Lycagon that put this Mark on me.

21:08.750 --> 21:13.250
And now that I've defeated her,
that means it's getting removed!

21:14.500 --> 21:18.630
I didn't even need to ask that saint lady!

21:18.630 --> 21:22.260
My days of going around
half-naked are finally over!

21:22.890 --> 21:26.890
Since this is the last time,
I should say farewell to my "freak" look!

21:29.890 --> 21:31.040
STARING BIRD MASK
EQUIPPED

21:31.040 --> 21:34.490
Well, since I've been wearing this
for so long, I got quite attached to it.

21:34.490 --> 21:36.780
So you're aware that it
makes you look like a freak?

21:39.110 --> 21:44.910
All right! Bring it on!
Take this accursed mark off me!

21:50.540 --> 21:51.540
Huh?

21:58.800 --> 21:59.920
Huh?

22:04.930 --> 22:10.890
What?!
